Portions of boundary.py are a Python port of AMFlow.cpp
(https://github.com/chang18/amflow-cpp), Copyright (c) 2026 AMFlow.cpp
contributors, released under the MIT License. The ported routines are the
five-entry single-mass vacuum table with its lookup (qft::vacuum and
qft::vacuum_known, src/qft/vacuum.cpp), the SingleMass Gamma prefactor
(compute_single_mass_prefactor, src/pipeline/amfsystem.cpp) and the
ending-value rule (try_builtin_ending_value, src/pipeline/amfsystem.cpp).
boundary.py cites the source lines it follows. The upstream notice is
